ice their height. D and E have unequal patterned bars. In B the unshaded bar is shorter than the patterned bars, while in A it is taller but less than twice as tall. C has exactly the required proportions, so the answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).","id":"compare-category-shares","label":"Match the proportions","legacyRouteId":"compare-category-shares","provenance":{"evidence":[{"label":"Accepted primary worked-solution review","path":"../database/knowledge-graph/evidence/solutions-2026-11-07-by-era/1993_AMC_8_Q05.json","sha256":"b3b8abad1e8d1acaddf48df3d1e13f0bbc0bbd12a67ff438bba45e5293d3948a"}],"license":"CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0","licenseURL":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/","reviewStatus":"AI-authored and independently AI-reviewed; not teacher reviewed","source":"Original Math Practice solution","sourceRef":"amc/1993_AMC_8_Q05#compare-category-shares","sourceURL":"https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice"}}],"solutionOmittedReason":"","solutionSource":"Original Math Practice solution","solutionSourceURL":"https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice","solutionStatus":"AI-authored and independently AI-reviewed; not teacher reviewed","sourceInfo":{"attribution":"American Mathematics Competitions (AMC), Mathematical Association of America (MAA)","kind":"question","label":"1993_AMC_8_Q05","license":"CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0","licenseURL":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/","position":{"batch":"NA","level":"AMC 8","number":5,"year":1993},"sourceURL":"https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/1993/solutions"},"sourceRef":"amc/1993_AMC_8_Q05","sourceURL":"https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/1993/solutions","topic":{"id":"NA","label":"NA"},"translationStatus":"","unorderedAnswers":false,"year":1993}
